<div class="row">
  <div class="col-lg-12">
    <div class="jumbotron bg-light p-5 rounded">
      <h1 class="display-4">Welcome to BrawoCMS</h1>
      <p class="lead">A flexible, developer-friendly CMS engine for Rails applications</p>
      <hr class="my-4">
      <p>This is a demo application showcasing the BrawoCMS engine capabilities.</p>
      <p>
        <%= link_to "View Articles", articles_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg" %>
        <%= link_to "View Products", products_path, class: "btn btn-success btn-lg" %>
        <%= link_to "Admin Panel", brawo_cms.admin_root_path, class: "btn btn-warning btn-lg" %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-5">
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <%= render FeatureCardComponent.new(
          title: "📝 Articles",
          body: "Manage blog posts, news articles, and editorial content with custom fields.",
          link_text: "Browse Articles",
          url: articles_path,
          button_class: "btn-primary"
        ) %>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <%= render FeatureCardComponent.new(
          title: "🛍️ Products",
          body: "Create and manage product catalogs with pricing, inventory, and descriptions.",
          link_text: "Browse Products",
          url: products_path,
          button_class: "btn-success"
        ) %>
  </div>
  <div class="col-md-4">
    <%= render FeatureCardComponent.new(
          title: "⚙️ Admin Panel",
          body: "Access the CMS admin interface to create and manage all content types.",
          link_text: "Go to Admin",
          url: brawo_cms.admin_root_path,
          button_class: "btn-warning"
        ) %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="row mt-5">
  <div class="col-lg-12">
    <h3>How to Use BrawoCMS in Your App</h3>
    <p>Creating a new content type is easy. Here's how the Article model in this demo was created:</p>

    <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>class Article < BrawoCms::Content
  include BrawoCms::ContentTypeable

  content_type :article,
    label: 'Article',
    fields: [
      { name: :author, type: :string, label: 'Author' },
      { name: :body, type: :textarea, label: 'Article Body' },
      { name: :published_date, type: :date, label: 'Publish Date' },
      { name: :featured, type: :boolean, label: 'Featured Article' },
      { name: :category, type: :select, label: 'Category',
        choices: [['Technology', 'tech'], ['Business', 'business']] }
    ]
end</code></pre>

    <p class="mt-3">Or use the generator:</p>
    <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3 rounded"><code>rails generate brawo_cms:content_type Article author:string body:textarea published_date:date</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
